      "scene_count": 21,
      "scenes": [
        {
          "effective_query": "bathroom mirror at night, reflection leaning on sink, single bulb",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 0,
          "original_query": "bathroom mirror at night, reflection leaning on sink, single bulb",
          "primary_symbol": "bathroom mirror at night",
          "query_family": "perception",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "bathroom mirror at night, reflection",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "Look at you. Three in the morning again, wide awake, chest tight, scanning for what's wrong. Can we talk about that alarm going off in you? Because I don't think it means what you think it means.",
          "visual_function": "hook"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 1,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "cinematic still photograph, moody",
          "query_family": "nature",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "cinematic still photograph, moody lighting",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "Right now, somewhere in your body, there's a signal firing. You've been treating it like a prophecy. Like it knows something. That's the first thing we need to look at together.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "old house hallway at night, warm lamp, long shadows",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 2,
          "original_query": "old house hallway at night, warm lamp, long shadows",
          "primary_symbol": "old house hallway at",
          "query_family": "architecture",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "old house hallway at night",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "Your alarm system was installed a long time ago. And here's what nobody told you: it was never built to be accurate. It was built to be early.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 3,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "minimal flat design schematic",
          "query_family": "object_tool",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "minimal flat design schematic, dark",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "The part of you that fires that signal can't tell a real threat from a remembered one. It reacts to burnt toast and housefires with the same siren. A false alarm bias, wired in early. It may be why your line survived.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "hand hesitating over glowing phone screen in dark room",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": true,
          "human_role": "observer",
          "index": 4,
          "original_query": "hand hesitating over glowing phone screen in dark room",
          "primary_symbol": "hand hesitating over glowing",
          "query_family": "object_tool",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "hand hesitating over glowing phone",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "Watch yourself today. The email that made your stomach drop. The pause before you opened it. That wasn't danger. That was the siren doing what sirens do.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 5,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "psychedelic flowing visual, alarm-red",
          "query_family": "geometry",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "psychedelic flowing visual, alarm-red waves",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "And here's where it gets strange. The alarm doesn't just report your world. It colors it. Once it fires, everything looks like evidence. The feeling paints the room.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "door lock being tested at night, kitchen kettle steam, restless pacing shadow",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 6,
          "original_query": "door lock being tested at night, kitchen kettle steam, restless pacing shadow",
          "primary_symbol": "door lock being tested",
          "query_family": "architecture",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "door lock being tested at",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "So you check the locks again. Reread the text again. Rehearse the conversation again. Not because there's fire. Because checking is what the alarm asks for. And every check tells it the alarm was right.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 7,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "minimal flat design schematic",
          "query_family": "pathway",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "minimal flat design schematic, dark",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "That loop has a shape. Alarm. Check. Relief. And the relief trains the alarm to fire sooner next time. You haven't been calming it. You may have been training it.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 8,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "cinematic still photograph, moody",
          "query_family": "nature",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "cinematic still photograph, moody lighting",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "Now the real question. Who set your sensitivity? Because you didn't. Somebody taught your system what counts as smoke. A loud house. A quiet leaving. A year nobody explained.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "staircase at night from low angle, warm light under a door",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 9,
          "original_query": "staircase at night from low angle, warm light under a door",
          "primary_symbol": "staircase at night from",
          "query_family": "architecture",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "staircase at night from low",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "Some of your alarms were calibrated by a childhood that needed them. Back then, reading a room fast mattered. Hearing footsteps mattered. Your sensitivity was intelligence. It kept a smaller you safe.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "calm sunlit apartment morning, curtains moving, coffee steam",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 10,
          "original_query": "calm sunlit apartment morning, curtains moving, coffee steam",
          "primary_symbol": "calm sunlit apartment morning",
          "query_family": "object_tool",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "calm sunlit apartment morning, curtains",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "But look around. You're not there anymore. The alarm is still guarding a house you moved out of years ago. It never got the memo. That's not damage. That's devotion with an old map.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 11,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "psychedelic flowing visual, chaotic",
          "query_family": "geometry",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "psychedelic flowing visual, chaotic red",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "So what do you do with an alarm you can't argue with? You stop arguing. You don't debate a siren. You check the kitchen.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "slow breath by a window, hand flat on chest, morning light",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": true,
          "human_role": "observer",
          "index": 12,
          "original_query": "slow breath by a window, hand flat on chest, morning light",
          "primary_symbol": "slow breath by a",
          "query_family": "architecture",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "slow breath by a window",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "Next time it fires, try this. Don't ask, what if it's right. Ask, what would I see if I actually looked? Then look. Slowly. Like someone checking a kitchen, not fleeing a fire.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 13,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "minimal flat design schematic",
          "query_family": "object_tool",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "minimal flat design schematic, dark",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "The alarm says everything. The kitchen shows toast, most days. Keep the score if you have to. Ten alarms. How many fires? Your own data will out-argue your fear better than I ever could.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "two friends laughing quietly at a kitchen table, easy body language",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 14,
          "original_query": "two friends laughing quietly at a kitchen table, easy body language",
          "primary_symbol": "two friends laughing quietly",
          "query_family": "object_tool",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "two friends laughing quietly at",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "And when it's toast, and it will mostly be toast, you don't punish the detector. You thank it. It's not broken. It's early. There's a difference, and the difference is the whole thing.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 15,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "ceiling alarm device green",
          "query_family": "architecture",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "cinematic still photograph, moody lighting",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "Some alarms you'll recalibrate. Some you'll just stop obeying. Both count. The goal was never silence. A house with no detector isn't peaceful. It's unprotected. You want a detector you can live with.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 16,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "psychedelic flowing visual, vast",
          "query_family": "nature",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "psychedelic flowing visual, vast calm",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "There may be a day the siren fires and it's real. And here's what the practice buys you: a self that can tell the difference. That self moves faster than panic ever did.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "bedroom at night, person sitting up calmly, soft dark blue light",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": true,
          "human_role": "observer",
          "index": 17,
          "original_query": "bedroom at night, person sitting up calmly, soft dark blue light",
          "primary_symbol": "bedroom at night, person",
          "query_family": "human",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "bedroom at night, person sitting",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "So. Back to three in the morning. The tightness comes. And this time you say: I hear you. I'm checking. And you look, and the room is just a room, and the night is just a night.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 18,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "minimal flat design schematic",
          "query_family": "object_tool",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "minimal flat design schematic, dark",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "You were never broken for having a loud alarm. You were unsupervised with it. That ends when you start doing the checking.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "person opening curtains to full daylight, rooms brightening",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": true,
          "human_role": "unspecified",
          "index": 19,
          "original_query": "person opening curtains to full daylight, rooms brightening",
          "primary_symbol": "person opening curtains to",
          "query_family": "transformation",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "person opening curtains to full",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "Which alarms in your house are set too sensitive? And who set them? Don't answer fast. Walk your rooms this week. Listen for which sirens are guarding fires that went out years ago.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        },
        {
          "effective_query": "",
          "generic_human": false,
          "human_present": false,
          "human_role": null,
          "index": 20,
          "original_query": null,
          "primary_symbol": "cinematic still photograph, moody",
          "query_family": "architecture",
          "selected_family": null,
          "semantic_anchor": "cinematic still photograph, moody lighting",
          "symbol_family": "object_tool",
          "text": "This is The Reality Machine. If this one found you at the right alarm, you know where we are. Come back anytime. We check kitchens here.",
          "visual_function": "witness"
        }
      ],
